=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
There is no fault in this network. A live ping from pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) to pc_0_1
(10.0.1.2) completes with 5/5 packets delivered and ~1.5 ms average RTT. Every
BGP route needed for end-to-end connectivity is correctly installed and active in
the FIB of every device in the fabric.

The team's assumption that super_spine_router_0 is "black-holing" east-west
traffic is architecturally unfounded. In a 3-tier Clos/BGP fabric like this one,
intra-fabric rack-to-rack traffic travels via the spine layer only — not the
super-spine. The TTL of 61 received at pc_0_1 (Linux default start TTL 64,
decremented once per router hop) confirms the actual forwarding path is
leaf_router_0_0 → spine_router_0_0 → leaf_router_0_1, three hops, with
super_spine_router_0 never touched. Super-spine devices in a Clos fabric handle
north-south or inter-pod traffic; their absence from intra-pod forwarding is
correct by design.

super_spine_router_0 is itself healthy: its BGP sessions with spine_router_0_0
(AS 65100) and spine_router_0_1 (AS 65101) are established, and it has learned
both 10.0.0.0/24 and 10.0.1.0/24 correctly. No route leak, no null route, no
policy drop, no missing advertisement was found anywhere in the fabric.

Root cause: There is no fault — the reported symptom does not exist in the
current lab state; the helpdesk ticket is based on a false premise.

Corrective action: No device needs to be restarted. The operations team should
re-verify connectivity from the end-host itself and close the ticket as
"no fault found / false alarm."
=== END ===
